\end{equation}

In fact, \autoref{factor} holds for all $N\leq k\leq t-2$. Indeed, if $t-N\leq k\leq t-2$, then by the assumption of the lemma, it must be that $\xi_{k+1}=0$. In this case, \autoref{factor} reduces to $1_{n}=U[\sigma^{n}_{t-1,n}]^{2}$, which holds by \autoref{commuting perms}. 

Therefore,  
$$
\begin{aligned}
