\end{aligned}
$$
Define $B(y):=\{1\leq k\leq n_{i}:y\in B_{i,k}\}$. By \autoref{Bik}, $B(y)=\{1=k_{1}<\cdots<k_{s}\}$, where $k_{t}= 1+n_{i_{1}}+\cdots+n_{i_{t-1}}$ for $1\leq t\leq s$. Set $k_{s+1}:=n_{i}+1$ and note that $k_{t+1}-k_{t}=n_{i_{t}}$ for all $1\leq t\leq s$. By assumption $n_{i}\geq\mathfrak{s}(A)>N$, and so, in light of (I) and (III) above, we may apply \autoref{Wn reduction} with the vector $(\Theta_{i}(y)_{1,1},\ldots,\Theta_{i}(y)_{n_{i},n_{i}})$ and the set $B(y)$, to obtain
