\end{aligned}.
$$
For $1\leq j\leq q$, we have $h^{\beta_{j}}(x)\in S$ by property (2) above, so that $g(h^{\beta_{j}}(x))=0$. Hence, partitioning $\{1,2,\ldots,n_{i}^{R}\}$ into the sets $\{\beta_{j-1}+1,\ldots,\beta_{j}\}$ for $1\leq j\leq q$, we may view $\gamma_{R}(ug)_{i}(x)$ as a block-diagonal matrix $\operatorname{diag}(B_{1},\ldots,B_{q})$, where
$$
\begin{aligned}
B_{j}&:=\begin{pmatrix}
0 & & & & \\
