& & \ddots & 0 &\\
& & & g(h^{\beta_{j}-1}(x)) & 0
\end{pmatrix}







=\gamma_{S}(ug)_{i_{j}}(h^{\beta_{j-1}}(x)),
\end{aligned}
$$
which yields \autoref{diagonal ug}.

We have shown that $x$ decomposes into $h^{\beta_{0}}(x)=x,h^{\beta_{1}}(x),\ldots,h^{\beta_{q-1}}(x)$ under $\psi$ on the generators of $A_{S}$. Let us now use continuity to prove that this decomposition is maintained for all elements of $A_{S}$. Let $a\in A_{S}$ be arbitrary. By definition, we may write $a=\lim_{n\to\infty}w_{n}$, where for each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $w_{n}$ is a word in $C(T)\cup uC_{0}(T\setminus S)\cup C_{0}(T\setminus S)u^{*}$. By \autoref{diagonal f} and \autoref{diagonal ug}, 
